6:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"how are answer sets curated?"}]}]
7:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"By aggregating datasets (dictionaries, wiki pages, encyclopedias, whatever sources the question calls for), then merging and cleaning the result into one answer set."}]}]
8:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"how is rarity determined?"}]}]
9:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Depends on the question. Some prompts can be scored entirely mechanically against a familiarity database of how often a word or name actually turns up in what people read and write. Others can’t be reduced to a number like that, and those get a combination of LLM assistance and a manual pass."}]}]
a:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"why is the krillion sometimes less rare than some deep cuts?"}]}]
b:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Because the Krillion isn’t chosen on rarity alone. Past a certain depth, rarity gets hard to disambiguate, so the gem is also picked for fun factor: the answer that’s most satisfying to land on. That might sound like it defeats the point, but some of the answers collected are so obscure that maybe one of you would ever type them. The gem should be something at least a few of you actually get."}]}]
c:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"why was my answer not listed?"}]}]
d:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Because I didn’t find it, sorry. Sometimes I miss a source, which is usually why a fair answer is missing. I’m trying to make sure this happens as rarely as possible."}]}]
e:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"why is autocorrect so generous?"}]}]
f:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Some questions have thousands of accepted answers, and many of those answers have aliases because people use different names for the same thing. Autocorrect checks those aliases too, so being a letter or two off one of them can turn your guess into something you weren’t expecting."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"For example, Threebanded Sheephead has “sea donkey” as an alias. That’s only one letter off “sea monkey,” even though “sea monkey” and “Threebanded Sheephead” look nothing alike."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"I try to catch and prevent these weird matches as much as possible, but that’s why they happen."}]]}]
10:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Why does the Puffer Party timer feel random?"}]}]
11:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"It’s actually the length of the hidden fuse that’s random, between 10 and 30 seconds under the default settings. That timer is shared across the room and keeps counting down as the puffer gets passed around. If there are 20 seconds left when you pass it, the next person inherits those 20 seconds. If there are fewer than 8 seconds left, it goes back to 8. After a pop, a new random fuse starts."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"The idea was to make it something like hot potato, and I also took inspiration from JKLM’s BombParty."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"I see y’all’s complaints about this, and yeah, the timer’s randomness is intentional, not a glitch. Open to your thoughts though. If you think this needs a redesign, make a post on the subreddit referencing this FAQ section and I’ll assess."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Sometimes, though, intermittent server lag or your own Wi-Fi lag can make it look like the puffer’s still going on your screen when it's already the next turn or it's popped."}]]}]
12:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"do purchases remove ads?"}]}]
13:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. Any unlock, for any pack, turns ads off across the whole site. Link your Google account and it comes with you to other devices."}]}]
14:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"is krillion developed by a team?"}]}]
15:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"No, just me."}]}]
16:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Who are you"}]}]
17:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"I’m kp, the person behind Krillion. The name’s just a pseudonym for now. I’m only putting this here because other people are claiming to be me, and Google’s AI search is currently listing some random dude who made a copycat clone as Krillion’s creator."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"If you’re curious about me, I’m a 23-year-old American CS grad."}]]}]
18:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"can we work together?"}]}]
19:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":["For partnerships, collaborations, or other business inquiries, email"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"mailto:business@krillion.io","className":"underline text-drift hover:text-lumen-cyan","children":"business@krillion.io"}],"."]}]}]
1a:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"are you going to make an app?"}]}]
1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":["Eventually, yes. If you have ideas for what it should be, email"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"mailto:support@krillion.io","className":"underline text-drift hover:text-lumen-cyan","children":"support@krillion.io"}],"."]}]}]
1c:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"do you have merch?"}]}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":["Yep. Check out the"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://shop.krillion.io/","className":"underline text-drift hover:text-lumen-cyan","children":"merch store"}],"."]}]}]
1e:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"are you going to make krillion multiplayer?"}]}]
1f:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Eventually, yes. There’s also a party game based on Krillion in the planning stages."}]}]
20:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"what is “too clever”?"}]}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"The go-to “obscure” pick that isn’t actually that obscure."}]}]
22:["$","h2",null,{"className":"fathom mt-10 mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"are you releasing more packs?"}]}]
23:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4 mb-10","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-drift leading-relaxed","children":"Yes, but right now the focus is on perfecting answer set curation and rarity selection. New packs come after that."}]}]
